+# Windows / CUDA 11.8 / V100 (sm_70) build
+
+Scope: branch `v100-upstream` (upstream engine 0.1.21 + the V100 / CUDA 11.8 port below), for machines whose NVIDIA
+driver tops out at CUDA 11.x (tested on driver 472.12, Tesla V100 16 GB). Nothing in the upstream 0.1.21 feature set
+(conversation cache, AVX2 i-quant kernels, Q4_0 KV, multi-GPU layer split) is changed by this port; V100-specific
+limits are listed at the end. Upstream's own requirements (RTX 30/40/50, current driver) still apply to anything
+outside this branch.
+
+## Port changes on this branch (vs upstream 0.1.21)
+
+- CUDA standard 17 for nvcc 11.8 (nvcc 11.8 accepts at most C++17); host C++ stays at 20.
+- `cudaGraphInstantiate` rewritten from the CUDA 12 3-argument form to the CUDA 11.8 5-argument form.
+- `setup.py`: Volta (sm_70) builds locally with CUDA 11.8 (nvcc 11.8 is the last one emitting sm_70; the V100 box runs
+  driver 472) with `nvidia-*-cu11` pip wheels and minimum driver 452; sm_80+ keeps upstream's CUDA 13 path.
+- Kernels: IQ4_XS (type 23) in `native_expert_grouped` (needed by GSQ-RCO IQ3_S), and `gather_rows` for rows that are
+  not 16-byte multiples (the IQ3_S MTP head row is 2100 B). Covered by `native_expert_parity --selftest` (ctest).
+
+## Toolchain
+
+- CUDA 11.8 (`nvcc`), MSVC 14.34 (VS 2022 Build Tools), Ninja, CMake
+- `CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=70`, `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`
+
+Build with the wrapper script (output `H:\qwen38-v100\build-strata-up\strata.exe`):
+
+```bat
+cmd /c H:\qwen38-v100\scripts\build-strata-up.bat
+```
+
+Manual equivalent (same flags as the script — without `-DSTRATA_ENABLE_CUDA=ON` the build is CPU-only,
+and without `-DSTRATA_GGML_DIR` CMake tries to fetch ggml from the network):
+
+```bat
+call "C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\BuildTools\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvars64.bat" -vcvars_ver=14.34
+set PATH=C:\llm-local\cuda-11.8\bin;%PATH%
+cmake -S H:\qwen38-v100\strata-up -B H:\qwen38-v100\build-strata-up -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DSTRATA_ENABLE_CUDA=ON -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=70 -DCMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER=C:/llm-local/cuda-11.8/bin/nvcc.exe -DCUDAToolkit_ROOT=C:/llm-local/cuda-11.8 -DSTRATA_GGML_DIR=H:/qwen38-v100/llama-pinned
+cmake --build H:\qwen38-v100\build-strata-up
+ctest --test-dir H:\qwen38-v100\build-strata-up
+```
+
+Step-1 status on this branch: `native_expert_parity --selftest` passes; ctest 22/24 pass — the 2 failures are absent
+PLE fixtures and Windows privilege 1314, not code failures.
+
+## Measured (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, ISTA-DASLab GSQ-RCO Q2_0, V100 16GB + DDR4 host)
+
+Measured on the earlier `win-cuda118` fork (same machine, older engine base); re-measurement on 0.1.21 is pending.
+
+`--expert-cache 7500 --prefill 2048 --spec 4 --spec-min-p 0.5 --mtp <q2_0 rt> --max-context 8192`, Swift expert profile:
+
+| | tok/s |
+|---|---|
+| decode | 51.0 / 53.0 / 51.8 |
+| prefill (2047 tokens) | 541 – 547 |
+
+At `--max-context 131072 --kv int8` the largest expert cache that starts and serves is 6400 slots (VRAM 16.19 / 16.26 GB). A 30k-token needle test answered correctly.
+
+The MTP runtime pack was built with `STRATA_GGUF_PY` pointing at a llama.cpp `gguf-py` checkout.
+
+## GSQ-RCO IQ3_S (3.5 bpw) and the clock sweet spot
+
+Same provenance as above (earlier fork, same machine). Cache sizes that start: 3500 slots at 8K, 2800 at
+`--max-context 131072 --kv int8`.
+
+One pelican-SVG generation per point, GPU clock locked for the measurement, energy from 2 Hz GPU power samples:
+
+| quant | clock | tok/s | J/token (GPU) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Q2_0 | 600 MHz | 34.9 | 1.44 |
+| Q2_0 | 900 MHz | 47.6 | 1.22 |
+| Q2_0 | 1500 MHz | 62.3 | 1.87 |
+| IQ3_S | 600 MHz | 26.3 | 1.89 |
+| IQ3_S | 900 MHz | 34.5 | 1.60 |
+
+Observed sweet spot was ~900 MHz: Q2_0 kept 76 % of the stock-boost speed (47.6 vs 62.3 tok/s) for 65 % of the GPU
+energy per token (1.22 vs 1.87 J), ~55 W average, ~54 °C. Going lower (600 MHz) cost speed without saving energy per
+token. Decode here is bound by expert traffic over PCIe and host RAM, so the top clocks buy relatively little.
+
+IQ3_S matched a Q4_K_XL llama.cpp baseline on our small math (15/15) and code (8/8) sets; Q2_0 lost visibly on SVG
+drawing.
+
+## Branch-specific limitations (not upstream behavior)
+
+- No ready-made sm_70 engine: `setup.py`'s `PREBUILT_URL` points at upstream (Niko1221), whose single-asset
+  0.1.21 prebuilt has no sm_70 build, so on a V100 setup compiles the engine locally with CUDA 11.8 (or pass
+  `--prebuilt` / `STRATA_PREBUILT_URL` pointing at a compatible sm_70 asset explicitly).
+- Answer **no** to "Images?": the vision helper is not tested on sm_70 yet.
+- Upstream 0.1.21's multi-GPU layer split is unvalidated on V100 (a second V100 is expected; until then, single-GPU).
+- Upstream's conversation cache (`--prompt-cache`, see `src/program/generate.cpp` `ConvCheckpoint` and
+  `include/strata/program/conv_cache.hpp`) is evaluated separately; the fork's own prefix-cache series was
+  deliberately not ported (see the merge report in `H:\qwen38-v100\briefs\REPORT-UPSTREAM-MERGE.md`).
